# LLVM-123t: single-rounding fused multiply-add end-to-end.
#
# `llvm.fma` / C `fma`/`fmaf` must lower to ONE `fofma`/`ftfma`
# (contract-fp.md §fma = SimRISC-07 §2.5: rfHA <- rfHB * rfHC + rfHD, single
# rounding) -- never to the two-step `fomul` + `foadd`.  The guest program
# tests inputs whose exact a*b+c is representable, so the fused and two-step
# results provably differ:
#     f64: (1+2^-52)^2 - (1+2^-51) = 2^-104 (fused) vs 0 (two-step)
#     f32: (1+2^-23)^2 - (1+2^-22) = 2^-46  (fused) vs 0 (two-step)
# The guest exit code is the test result (0 = all checks pass).
#
# The DADAO toolchain is bare metal: no errno, so `-fmath-errno` is off by
# default and clang forms the LLVM intrinsic (`fma` -> llvm.fma) instead of an
# out-of-line libm call.  The assembly checks below pin that: a non-zero
# `jump [rb0, fma]` count would mean the call path came back.
#
# RUN: %clang -target dadao-unknown-elf -nostdlib -O2 -S %e2e_dir/fma_e2e.c -o %t.s
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ASM < %t.s
# RUN: %not grep -q 'jump \[rb0, fma' %t.s
# RUN: grep -q fomul %t.s
# RUN: grep -q foadd %t.s
# RUN: %clang -target dadao-unknown-elf -nostdlib -O2 -c %e2e_dir/fma_e2e.c -o %t.o
# RUN: %llvm_mc --triple=dadao-unknown-elf -filetype=obj %crt0 -o %t.crt0.o
# RUN: %ld -T %linker_script %t.crt0.o %t.o -o %t.elf
# RUN: timeout 30 %qemu -M dadao-m1 -kernel %t.elf -semihosting-config enable=on,target=native -display none -nographic

# One fofma in the f64 helper and one ftfma in the f32 helper, each with a
# distinct destination (three-address: no copy into the addend).
# ASM-LABEL: fma_d:
# ASM: fofma rf{{[0-9]+}}, rf{{[0-9]+}}, rf{{[0-9]+}}, rf{{[0-9]+}}
# ASM-LABEL: fma_f:
# ASM: ftfma rf{{[0-9]+}}, rf{{[0-9]+}}, rf{{[0-9]+}}, rf{{[0-9]+}}
